From 6afa2ef3240cf4e5859ee7a39344fd2ff93d8460 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Christopher Owen <3221756+christopherowen@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 22:25:17 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] perf(dsv41): warp-shuffle vocab greedy epilogue and L2-hot
 step dispatch

Upstream base: 19f2c20ed4d64ae22bd009ceacadd85e2a81e354.
Immediate base: a75357bba81e31e4f3085700f94b6a0b29aed44a.

Rationale:
1. Option B (Warp-shuffle MMA fragment epilogue): Replace full [block_M, 64]
   shared-memory staging (C_shared) and block-wide T.sync_threads() in
   bf16_vocab_markov_greedy_partials, packed_vocab_markov_greedy_partials,
   packed_vocab_greedy_partials, and nvfp4_vocab_greedy_partials with an
   in-register warp-shuffle (__shfl_xor_sync across MMA fragment lanes
   offset=2,1) reduction (vllm_vocab_tile_argmax_clocal) that writes only
   per-warp winners ([block_M, WARPS_N]) to shared memory and reduces them on
   tx < block_M. Reduces bf16_vocab_markov_greedy_partials register pressure
   from 126 to 43 registers and speeds up L2-hot Markov steps by up to
   -11.0% on TP3 and -16.9% on TP4 (12-bit packed) and -18.9% on BF16.
2. Option A (Step-aware L2-hot TP>1 dispatch + scratch reuse): On TP3/TP4,
   the 12-bit packed Markov W2 shard (16.55 MB / 12.40 MB) stays resident in
   GB10 L2 cache across draft steps pos = 1..4. Add
   _use_fused_markov_greedy_step(tp_size, step, num_reqs) in
   DSparkSpeculator._sample_sequential and persistent output buffer reuse in
   markov_bias_local / vocab.project_head(..., out=...) so L2-cold pos == 0
   (M >= 3) uses the fused kernel while L2-hot pos >= 1 (and M <= 2 on TP > 1)
   dispatches to unfused markov_bias_local + greedy_markov_shard_pair,
   reducing the 5-step Markov composite (cold0 + 4*hot) across M = 1..16 by
   -7.06 to -12.88 us on TP3 and -5.71 to -16.87 us on TP4.

Quality:
Bit-identical torch.equal greedy token and secondary draft selection across all
vocabulary head layouts (BF16, 12-bit packed, NVFP4) and TP sizes (TP1, TP3,
TP4), preserving NaN-first tie-breaking and lowest global vocabulary index
tie-breaking.

Tests:
72/72 vocab + PDL unit tests and 55/55 DSpark greedy Markov unit tests pass
across 2 GPU container boots on GB10 (SM121a) with 0 PDL violations, plus
2-boot cold/hot benchmark verification across M = 1..16 on TP1, TP3, and TP4.

Upstream status:
Local DeepSeek-V4.1 / DSpark TileLang optimization for spark-ds41f.
